0..79 Comment "//! `buffer-returned` returns an allocated buffer after a mock ring completion."
80..83 Comment "//!"
84..155 Comment "//! It keeps a buffer live exactly once from allocation to freeing. The"
156..228 Comment "//! pathological twin refuses a buffer that a program does not return as"
229..252 Comment "//! `BufferUnreturned`."
253..256 Comment "//!"
257..319 Comment "//! The kernel owns the buffer while an operation is in flight"
320..397 Comment "//! [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]. A `Ring.Eff` handler mints the buffer and"
398..475 Comment "//! handles its return. The mock kernel sends it back before the continuation"
476..488 Comment "//! resumes."
489..492 Comment "//!"
493..555 Comment "//! - see: corpus/pathological/completion/buffer-misused.gandr"
556..599 Comment "//! - cites: [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]"
600..603 Comment "//!"
604..703 Comment "//! [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]: https://without.boats/blog/io-uring/ \"boats, Notes on io-uring\""
705..748 Comment "// The native buffer a receive places live."
